WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.800
althistory: A guided tour.
Demo graph: The Engine Age — what if Babbage finished the Analytical Engine in 1843?

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:11.200
The workspace. Each graph opens on its timeline. Views on the left, tools along the top, filters on the right.

3
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:17.350
Timeline. Arcs group events into periods and sub-periods. Hover any event to see who did what, to whom, and when.

4
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:22.150
Inferred pressures. althistory reads clusters of events and infers the economic, social and political pressures behind them.

5
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:30.750
Causal graph. Every cause-and-effect link, weighted and typed. Pick a layout to reorganise the graph.

6
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:36.550
Actor perspective. Follow one actor through the history: what they did, and what was done to them.

7
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:40.950
Ingestion. Bring history in from Wikipedia, Wikidata or plain text.

8
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:45.550
Review before import. Nothing is written until you have reviewed it: edit or untick rows, then import the rest.

9
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:51.950
Graphs and branches. Keep many graphs side by side, and branch one to explore a counterfactual without touching the original.

10
00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:58.050
Script it, too. Everything in the interface is also a CLI command and an MCP tool for agents.
